# vew_component_version data source

Reads a component version using its project, parent component, and version
identifiers. Retired, failed, and other returned terminal versions stay visible.

Permission: project assignment and `clients/packaging/component.read`.

## Selectors

| Attribute | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `project_id` | string | Required VEW project identifier. |
| `component_id` | string | Required parent component identifier. |
| `version_id` | string | Required exact component-version identifier. |

## Computed attributes

`description`, `definition_json`, `dependencies`, `software_vendor`,
`software_version`, nullable `license_dashboard` and `notes`, `name`, `status`,
`created_at`, `created_by`, `updated_at`, and `updated_by`. Each dependency
contains `component_id`, `component_name`, `version_id`, `version_name`, `type`,
`order`, and nullable `position`; the list follows dependency order. The
definition is canonical JSON. VEW does not return create-time release type, so
the data source has no `release_type` attribute. The full definition is stored
in Terraform state and may be present in plans and state backups.

```hcl
data "vew_component_version" "existing" {
  project_id   = var.project_id
  component_id = var.component_id
  version_id   = var.version_id
}

output "component_version_status" {
  value = data.vew_component_version.existing.status
}
```

